{%- comment -%}
  PDP: a gallery + buy bar layout with a 2-col info list. Ground-up
  markup; only the JS-contract hooks are carried across revisions —
  [data-product-root], #product-json, .pdp__gallery,
  .gallery-item[data-colors], .pdp__thumb, [data-atc], [data-opt-btn],
  [data-opt-current], [data-price],
  [data-gallery-dots], #zoom-dialog, [data-open-size-chart]/
  #size-chart-dialog, .opt/.sizes/.size-btn/.swatches/.swatch (theme.js reads
  those class names, and the quick-view dialog reuses their styling).

  THE ATC:
    MOBILE  — unchanged. The fixed bottom bar is the only add button, present
              from page load, reading "SELECT A SIZE" until a size is picked.
    DESKTOP — the buy column owns the primary black ATC (.pdp__atc), accepted
              payment marks sit under it, and the bottom bar turns into the
              RICH bar (thumbnail · name · colour · price · inline size row ·
              ink add block) that only appears once the column has scrolled out
              of view.
  All three add buttons carry [data-atc] and theme.js paints every one of them
  from the same render() pass — there is no second source of truth.

  Scarcity and live viewers are setting-owned and disappear when cleared.
  Delivery estimates stay off: the dated card below promises only a
  policy-matched SHIPPING date. Model measurements (models are AI-generated)
  and unverified natural-fibre claims stay off too.

  The newsletter popup is theme-owned, rendered from layout/theme.liquid
  (snippets/newsletter-popup.liquid + initNewsletterPopup in theme.js). It
  stays disabled INSIDE this section — the PDP itself stays popup-free, and
  the newsletter dialog never auto-opens over an open size sheet or bag.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  comment
    colour option index, hoisted above the initial-variant pick because that
    pick now needs it. Every image of a colour (not just the variant's featured
    one) is tagged from its alt text (" in <Colour>," / " in <Colour>-"), with
    the variant featured-media link as the fallback; theme.js filters on it.
  endcomment
  assign color_opt_index = -1
  assign color_values = '' | split: ''
  for option in product.options_with_values
    assign g_opt_down = option.name | downcase
    if g_opt_down == 'color' or g_opt_down == 'colour'
      assign color_opt_index = forloop.index0
      assign color_values = option.values
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    Initial variant: an explicit ?variant= keeps winning (selected_variant),
    otherwise the LEAD COLOUR wins — the colour of the first alt-tagged media,
    i.e. the photograph the PLP card just showed. selected_or_first_available
    follows variant (import) order, which can open a mismatched colour card.
    theme.js initPDP() and the quick-view open() apply the same rule.
  endcomment
  assign v = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  if product.selected_variant == nil and color_opt_index > -1
    assign lead_color = ''
    for m in product.media
      if m.media_type != 'image'
        continue
      endif
      assign m_lead_alt = m.alt | default: '' | downcase
      for cv in color_values
        assign cv_lead_down = cv | downcase
        assign lead_needle = ' in ' | append: cv_lead_down | append: ','
        assign lead_needle2 = ' in ' | append: cv_lead_down | append: '-'
        assign lead_needle3 = ' i ' | append: cv_lead_down | append: ','
        assign lead_needle4 = ' i ' | append: cv_lead_down | append: '-'
        if m_lead_alt contains lead_needle or m_lead_alt contains lead_needle2 or m_lead_alt contains lead_needle3 or m_lead_alt contains lead_needle4
          assign lead_color = cv
          break
        endif
      endfor
      if lead_color != ''
        break
      endif
    endfor
    if lead_color != ''
      for pv in product.variants
        if pv.available and pv.options[color_opt_index] == lead_color
          assign v = pv
          break
        endif
      endfor
    endif
  endif

  comment
    Full title shown as-is, pipe included — no name/descriptor split.
    pdp_descriptor stays as an always-blank variable so the richbar's elsif
    keeps compiling.
  endcomment
  assign pdp_name = product.title
  assign pdp_descriptor = ''

  comment
    Apparel guard, mirrored from theme.js initPDP(): a multi-value size option is
    NEVER pre-selected, so the bar opens on "Select a size" and the first paint
    matches what the JS renders a moment later (no label flash). An explicit
    ?variant= link keeps its size, exactly as the JS does.
  endcomment
  assign needs_size = false
  for option in product.options_with_values
    assign o_down = option.name | downcase
    if o_down contains 'size' and option.values.size > 1
      assign needs_size = true
    endif
  endfor
  if product.selected_variant
    assign needs_size = false
  endif
  comment
    Sizes are pre-selected — the needs_size computation above stays for
    reference, but the first paint matches theme.js: v (lead colour, first
    available size) is fully selected and every add button reads add-to-bag
    with a price.
  endcomment
  assign needs_size = false
  assign pdp_images = product.media | where: 'media_type', 'image'
  assign pdp_image_count = pdp_images.size
  assign pdp_price_pct = 0
  if v.compare_at_price > v.price
    assign pdp_price_pct = v.compare_at_price | minus: v.price | times: 100.0 | divided_by: v.compare_at_price | round
  endif
-%}
{%- comment -%} Description split: the first paragraph and the detail list are
kept separate so each can be styled deliberately, but both print exactly once
inside the Description info panel. Nothing from product.description remains
open under the buy buttons. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign desc_intro = '' -%}
{%- assign desc_rest = product.description -%}
{%- if product.description contains '</p>' -%}
  {%- assign desc_parts = product.description | split: '</p>' -%}
  {%- assign desc_intro = desc_parts | first | append: '</p>' -%}
  {%- assign intro_check = desc_intro | strip_html | strip -%}
  {%- if intro_check == blank -%}
    {%- assign desc_intro = '' -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign desc_rest = product.description | remove_first: desc_intro -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign details_check = desc_rest | strip_html | strip -%}

{%- capture size_chart_html -%}{{ product.metafields.custom.size_table }}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- if size_chart_html == blank -%}
  {%- capture size_chart_html -%}{{ section.settings.size_chart_default }}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- endif -%}

<section class="pdp" data-product-root>
  <div class="pdp__top">

    <div class="pdp__stage">
      {%- if pdp_image_count > 1 -%}
        <div class="pdp__rail" aria-label="{{ 'product.gallery.aria' | t }}">
          {%- for media in product.media -%}
            {%- if media.media_type == 'image' -%}
              {%- capture thumb_colors -%}{%- if color_opt_index > -1 -%}{%- assign tm_alt = media.alt | default: '' | downcase -%}{%- for cv in color_values -%}{%- assign cv_down = cv | downcase -%}{%- assign tneedle = ' in ' | append: cv_down | append: ',' -%}{%- assign tneedle2 = ' in ' | append: cv_down | append: '-' -%}{%- assign tneedle3 = ' i ' | append: cv_down | append: ',' -%}{%- assign tneedle4 = ' i ' | append: cv_down | append: '-' -%}{%- if tm_alt contains tneedle or tm_alt contains tneedle2 or tm_alt contains tneedle3 or tm_alt contains tneedle4 -%}{{ cv }}||{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endcapture -%}
              {%- if color_opt_index > -1 and thumb_colors == blank -%}{%- capture thumb_colors -%}{%- for pv in product.variants -%}{%- if pv.featured_media.id == media.id -%}{{ pv.options[color_opt_index] }}||{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}{%- endcapture -%}{%- endif -%}
              <button type="button" class="pdp__thumb" data-thumb-target="{{ media.id }}"{% if thumb_colors != blank %} data-colors="{{ thumb_colors | escape }}"{% endif %} aria-label="{{ 'product.gallery.show_image' | t: index: forloop.index }}">
                <img src="{{ media | image_url: width: 132 }}" width="66" height="99" loading="lazy" alt="">
              </button>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="pdp__frame">
        <div class="pdp__gallery">
          {%- for media in product.media -%}
            {%- if media.media_type == 'image' -%}
              {%- capture media_colors -%}{%- if color_opt_index > -1 -%}{%- assign m_alt = media.alt | default: '' | downcase -%}{%- for cv in color_values -%}{%- assign cv_down = cv | downcase -%}{%- assign needle = ' in ' | append: cv_down | append: ',' -%}{%- assign needle2 = ' in ' | append: cv_down | append: '-' -%}{%- assign needle3 = ' i ' | append: cv_down | append: ',' -%}{%- assign needle4 = ' i ' | append: cv_down | append: '-' -%}{%- if m_alt contains needle or m_alt contains needle2 or m_alt contains needle3 or m_alt contains needle4 -%}{{ cv }}||{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endcapture -%}
              {%- if color_opt_index > -1 and media_colors == blank -%}
                {%- capture media_colors -%}{%- for pv in product.variants -%}{%- if pv.featured_media.id == media.id -%}{{ pv.options[color_opt_index] }}||{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}{%- endcapture -%}
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- comment -%} ceiling 1024×1536: the masters are 2:3 at that size and Shopify
              silently DROPS the crop once the requested height exceeds the source, handing
              back an uncropped original at a different URL. The three srcset steps + sizes
              below must stay byte-identical to the preload in layout/theme.liquid or the
              hero image downloads twice. {%- endcomment -%}
              <button
                type="button"
                class="gallery-item{% if forloop.first %} is-current{% endif %}"
                data-media-id="{{ media.id }}"
                data-zoom-src="{{ media | image_url: width: 1024 }}"
                {% if media_colors != blank %}data-colors="{{ media_colors | escape }}"{% endif %}
                aria-label="{{ 'product.gallery.zoom_image' | t: index: forloop.index }}"
              >
                <img
                  src="{{ media | image_url: width: 800 }}"
                  srcset="{{ media | image_url: width: 500 }} 500w, {{ media | image_url: width: 640 }} 640w, {{ media | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w, {{ media | image_url: width: 1024 }} 1024w"
                  sizes="(max-width: 720px) 80vw, 46vw"
                  width="800" height="1200"
                  alt="{{ media.alt | default: product.title | escape }}"
                  {% if forloop.first %}fetchpriority="high"{% else %}loading="lazy"{% endif %}
                >
              </button>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
          {%- if pdp_image_count == 0 -%}
            {%- assign ph = product.id | modulo: 6 | plus: 1 -%}
            <div class="gallery-item is-current">{{ 'product-' | append: ph | placeholder_svg_tag }}</div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- comment -%} Dots and a visible "n / total" counter are omitted:
        with many images the dot row reads as a dotted rule across the
        photograph rather than as an indicator. The counter stays in the
        markup but visually hidden — it is the aria-live region that tells
        a screen-reader user which image they moved to, and the gallery has no
        other spoken position cue. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if pdp_image_count > 0 -%}<p class="visually-hidden" data-gallery-counter aria-live="polite">1 / {{ pdp_image_count }}</p>{%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="pdp__buy">
      {%- render 'pdp-rating' -%}
      {%- comment -%} Title block: NAME + descriptor on one row, price on its own
      row underneath, so the price never gets lost hard-right of the title. The
      colour moved onto the COLOR option label ("Color: Pink") further down —
      same [data-opt-current] hook, one line less. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="pdp__titles">
        <h1 class="pdp__name lbl">{{ pdp_name | escape }}</h1>
        {%- comment -%} descriptor sits BESIDE the name, not three rows below it {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if pdp_descriptor != blank -%}
          <p class="pdp__descriptor lbl-sm">{{ pdp_descriptor | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
      <div class="pdp__price lbl">
        <span data-price>
          {%- if v.compare_at_price > v.price -%}
            <s>{{ v.compare_at_price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</s> <span class="price--sale">{{ v.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
          {%- else -%}
            {{ v.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
        {%- comment -%} Sibling by contract: theme.js replaces every [data-price]
        innerHTML on a size click, so the real percentage badge must live outside it. {%- endcomment -%}
        <span data-price-badge{% if pdp_price_pct <= 0 %} hidden{% endif %}>{%- if pdp_price_pct > 0 -%}&minus;{{ pdp_price_pct }}%{%- endif -%}</span>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} The three-line USP stack under the price is gone. Its
      claims moved — secure payment closes the buy zone (one line over the
      payment marks), shipping + money-back sit as a two-point trust row under
      the accordions. Snippet + settings stay; re-adding means putting the
      render back here. {%- endcomment -%}

      {%- comment -%} The stock/urgency line sits between price and colour —
      not buried between fit scale and the buy zone. Viewers travels with it
      (its toggle needs a call site, ships OFF). {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- render 'pdp-scarcity', product: product -%}
      {%- render 'pdp-viewers', product: product -%}

      {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
        {%- for option in product.options_with_values -%}
          {%- assign opt_index = forloop.index0 -%}
          {%- assign opt_down = option.name | downcase -%}
          {%- assign is_color = false -%}
          {%- if opt_down == 'color' or opt_down == 'colour' -%}{%- assign is_color = true -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- if option.values.size < 2 -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- assign is_size = false -%}
          {%- if opt_down contains 'size' -%}{%- assign is_size = true -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- comment -%} Option NAME localisation: the option VALUE
          (v.options[opt_index], size_btn text, swatch value) is never touched
          here — the alt-text parser depends on those staying exactly as imported.
          Only the NAME ("Color"/"Size") routes through a locale key. {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign opt_label = option.name -%}
          {%- if is_color -%}
            {%- assign opt_label = 'product.option_color' | t -%}
          {%- elsif is_size -%}
            {%- assign opt_label = 'product.option_size' | t -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          <div class="opt"{% if is_size %} data-size-opt{% endif %}>
            {%- comment -%} SIZE head = label left, size-guide link right on the
            same row (saves an extra link row below the buttons). No value
            echo — the picked size shows on the selected button. Colour keeps
            its value (swatches carry no name). The finder lives inside the
            guide dialog. {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="opt__head">
              {%- if is_size -%}
                <p class="opt__label lbl-sm mute">{{ opt_label | upcase | escape }}</p>
                {%- if size_chart_html != blank -%}
                  <button type="button" class="tlink opt__guide" data-open-size-chart>{{ 'product.size.chart_link' | t }}</button>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- else -%}
                <p class="opt__label lbl-sm mute">{{ opt_label | upcase | escape }}: <strong class="opt__value" data-opt-current="{{ opt_index }}">{{ v.options[opt_index] | upcase | escape }}</strong></p>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
            {%- if is_color -%}
              <div class="swatches" role="group" aria-label="{{ opt_label | escape }}">
                {%- for value in option.values -%}
                  {%- comment -%} A colour is picked from its own photograph. The curated
                  alt-tagged media wins (same " in Colour," / " in Colour-" contract as
                  the gallery), variant featured media is only the fallback. {%- endcomment -%}
                  {%- assign cv_media = false -%}
                  {%- assign value_down = value | downcase -%}
                  {%- assign cv_needle = ' in ' | append: value_down | append: ',' -%}
                  {%- assign cv_needle2 = ' in ' | append: value_down | append: '-' -%}
                  {%- assign cv_needle3 = ' i ' | append: value_down | append: ',' -%}
                  {%- assign cv_needle4 = ' i ' | append: value_down | append: '-' -%}
                  {%- for cv_product_media in product.media -%}
                    {%- if cv_product_media.media_type == 'image' -%}
                      {%- assign cv_product_alt = cv_product_media.alt | default: '' | downcase -%}
                      {%- if cv_product_alt contains cv_needle or cv_product_alt contains cv_needle2 or cv_product_alt contains cv_needle3 or cv_product_alt contains cv_needle4 -%}
                        {%- assign cv_media = cv_product_media -%}
                        {%- break -%}
                      {%- endif -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                  {%- unless cv_media -%}
                  {%- for cv_variant in product.variants -%}
                    {%- if cv_variant.options[opt_index] == value and cv_variant.featured_media != blank -%}
                      {%- assign cv_media = cv_variant.featured_media -%}
                      {%- break -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                  {%- endunless -%}
                  {%- if cv_media -%}
                    <button type="button" class="swatch swatch--img" data-opt-btn data-opt-index="{{ opt_index }}" data-opt-value="{{ value | escape }}" aria-pressed="{% if v.options[opt_index] == value %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}" aria-label="{{ value | escape }}" title="{{ value | escape }}"><img src="{{ cv_media | image_url: width: 96, height: 144, crop: 'center' }}" srcset="{{ cv_media | image_url: width: 96, height: 144, crop: 'center' }} 2x, {{ cv_media | image_url: width: 144, height: 216, crop: 'center' }} 3x" width="48" height="72" alt="" loading="lazy"></button>
                  {%- else -%}
                    {%- comment -%} colourless in Liquid on purpose: theme.js paintSwatches()
                    fills these from qvSwatchMap, so the fashion-hex table lives in exactly
                    one place (the PLP cards and the quick view share it). {%- endcomment -%}
                    <button type="button" class="swatch" data-swatch="{{ value | escape }}" data-opt-btn data-opt-index="{{ opt_index }}" data-opt-value="{{ value | escape }}" aria-pressed="{% if v.options[opt_index] == value %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}" aria-label="{{ value | escape }}" title="{{ value | escape }}"></button>
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>
            {%- else -%}
              <div class="sizes" role="group" aria-label="{{ opt_label | escape }}">
                {%- for value in option.values -%}
                  <button type="button" class="size-btn" data-opt-btn data-opt-index="{{ opt_index }}" data-opt-value="{{ value | escape }}" aria-pressed="{% if needs_size %}false{% elsif v.options[opt_index] == value %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}">{{ value | escape }}</button>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
          {%- comment -%} return anchor: the bar's expansion panel MOVES this row into
          the sheet (no duplicate picker to keep in sync) and puts it back here. {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if is_size -%}<span data-size-home hidden></span>{%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endunless -%}

      {%- comment -%} Size recommender lives inside the option loop, above the
      size row — see the render inside the loop. It still applies its answer
      by clicking the real size button (never a second picker). {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%} FIT SCALE is toggle-owned; derivation from
      custom.fit_note is unchanged. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%} sizekit: fit scale sits in one bordered block. The
      measure note is no longer printed — the settings toggle stays but this
      template doesn't render it. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if settings.fit_scale_enabled -%}
        <div class="pdp-sizekit">
          {%- render 'pdp-fit-scale' -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} ORDER: size grid → size help + fit → scarcity → buy —
      the scarcity line sits directly against the button, not separated from
      it by fit scale and spacing.

      The viewers line is removed here: with scarcity, the drawer countdown
      and the tier upsell already live, a fourth pressure signal cost 30px
      that kept the add button below the 785px fold. The snippet and its CSS
      stay — re-adding the render line brings it back. {%- endcomment -%}

      {%- comment -%} THE desktop add button. This is the primary action from
      900px up — it replaces a floating payment button far from the size just
      picked; below that it never renders and the fixed bar stays THE buy
      button. It carries [data-atc] like every other add button in
      this theme, and theme.js paints all of them from the one render() pass. {%- endcomment -%}
      <button
        type="button"
        class="bar pdp__atc{% if needs_size %} bar--awaiting{% endif %}"
        data-atc
        data-variant-id="{% unless needs_size %}{{ v.id }}{% endunless %}"
        {% unless needs_size or v.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
      >
        <span data-atc-label>{% if needs_size %}{{ 'product.atc.select_size' | t }}{% elsif v.available %}{{ 'product.atc.add_to_bag' | t }}{% else %}{{ 'product.atc.sold_out' | t }}{% endif %}</span>
        <span data-atc-price>{% if v.available and needs_size == false %}{{ v.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}{% endif %}</span>
      </button>

      {%- comment -%} The secure-payment trust line above the payment marks
      reads the locale key on every language — the settings value carries
      different (longer) wording than what belongs here, and only the primary
      locale would otherwise read the setting raw (same locale-fallback
      architecture rule as the retired USP stack). The delivery timeline moved
      below the accordions. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign cp_sec = 'product.usp.secure' | t -%}
      {%- if cp_sec != blank -%}
        <p class="pdp-secure lbl-sm">{% render 'icon', name: 'lock', size: 15 %}<span>{{ cp_sec | escape }}</span></p>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if shop.enabled_payment_types.size > 0 -%}
        <div class="pdp-payments pdp-payments--column" aria-label="{{ 'general.accepted_payment_methods' | t }}">
          {%- for payment_type in shop.enabled_payment_types -%}{{ payment_type | payment_type_svg_tag }}{%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} Renders only while the tier discounts exist — with them off
      this is nothing at all. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- render 'pdp-usp-lines' -%}


      {%- comment -%} Buy-more upsell ladder. It follows the completed buy
      zone: the moment a shopper has decided on one piece is the moment a
      second one is easiest to sell. DISPLAY ONLY — it renders only while
      settings.qty_tiers_enabled is on, and that switch must stay off until
      the matching Shopify automatic discounts exist. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%} Bundle ladder condensed to one line — the tier bar in
      the drawer carries the full ladder at the moment it matters. qty/pct
      read dynamically from the first and last ladder step so the line can
      never contradict the settings. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if settings.qty_tiers_enabled and settings.qty_tiers != blank -%}
        {%- assign pb_tiers = settings.qty_tiers | remove: ' ' | split: ',' -%}
        {%- comment -%} Heading + auto-apply subline + one soft tile per step
        (percentage bold left, e.g. "from 2 items – 10% EXTRA off" muted
        right). Reads straight from settings.qty_tiers so the lines can never
        contradict the discounts. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="pdp__bundle-line">
          <p class="pdp__bundle-head">{{ 'product.bundle.heading' | t }}</p>
          <p class="pdp__bundle-note">{{ 'product.bundle.auto_note' | t }}</p>
          <ul class="pdp__bundle-tiers">
            {%- for pb_tier in pb_tiers -%}
              {%- assign pb_pair = pb_tier | split: ':' -%}
              <li><span class="pdp__bundle-pctcol">{{ pb_pair[1] }}%</span><span class="pdp__bundle-desc">{{ 'product.bundle.tier_text' | t: qty: pb_pair[0], pct: pb_pair[1] }}</span></li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} pdp-complete-look renders at the page end — cross-sell
      never sits inside the buy zone. {%- endcomment -%}

      {%- comment -%} desc_intro and desc_rest both render once, in the
      Description info panel below — neither renders here. {%- endcomment -%}

      {%- comment -%} pdp__facts block is removed here: fit_note already
      renders in the Size & fit tab and the benefit lives in the Product details
      bullets — the duplicate line pair under the description read as clutter.
      The metafields stay populated; only this render spot is gone. {%- endcomment -%}

  {%- liquid
    assign has_description_tab = true
    if desc_intro == blank and details_check == blank
      assign has_description_tab = false
    endif
  -%}
    {%- comment -%} The whole info block (accordions + trust duo +
    complete-look) lives INSIDE .pdp__buy so it sits in the right rail on
    desktop instead of a centered orphan column. Mobile order is unchanged
    (block still renders after the buy content). Same-order guarantee:
    accordions -> trust duo -> complete-look. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%} ACCORDIONS, not inline tab-links. Same native
  <details class="acc"> vocabulary as the homepage FAQ, so the CSS animation
  and the WebKit WAAPI fallback (theme.js initAccordions, global details.acc
  query) apply with zero new JS. Description ships open — it is the first
  thing a paid click wants. The old [data-info-tab] handler in theme.js is
  now unused on this page and harmless. {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="pdp__info pdp__info--acc wrap">
    <div class="pdp__acc bt">
      {%- if has_description_tab -%}
        {%- comment -%} Ships CLOSED like every other panel — quiet page,
        reader opens what they want. {%- endcomment -%}
        <details class="acc bb">
          <summary class="acc__q lbl">{{ 'product.tabs.description' | t }}<span class="acc__sign" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
          <div class="acc__body pdp-rte prose">
            {%- if desc_intro != blank -%}<div class="pdp__desc" data-pdp-desc>{{ desc_intro }}</div>{%- endif -%}
            {%- if details_check != blank -%}<div class="pdp__details">{{ desc_rest }}</div>{%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </details>
      {%- endif -%}
      <details class="acc bb">
        <summary class="acc__q lbl">{{ 'product.tabs.fabric' | t }}<span class="acc__sign" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="acc__body pdp-rte">
          {%- if product.metafields.custom.care != blank -%}
            {{ product.metafields.custom.care }}
          {%- else -%}
            {{ section.settings.care_default }}
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="acc bb">
        <summary class="acc__q lbl">{{ 'product.tabs.fit' | t }}<span class="acc__sign" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="acc__body pdp-rte">
          {%- if product.metafields.custom.fit_note != blank -%}
            <p>{{ product.metafields.custom.fit_note | escape }}</p>
          {%- else -%}
            <p>{{ 'product.fit.true_to_size' | t }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- comment -%} custom.model_note prints verbatim and stays hidden
          while empty. Standing rule: models are AI-generated, so any
          measurement or model-size claim in this metafield would be
          fabricated. Fit guidance belongs in custom.fit_note. {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if product.metafields.custom.model_note != blank -%}
            <p>{{ product.metafields.custom.model_note | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if size_chart_html != blank -%}
            <p><button type="button" class="tlink" data-open-size-chart>{{ 'product.size.guide' | t }}</button></p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.enable_size_recommendation and size_chart_html != blank -%}
            <p><button type="button" class="tlink" data-open-size-rec>{{ 'product.size.find_my_size' | t }}</button></p>
          {%- endif -%}
          <p><a href="/policies/refund-policy">{{ 'product.returns.doesnt_fit' | t }}</a></p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="acc bb">
        <summary class="acc__q lbl">{{ 'product.tabs.shipping' | t }}<span class="acc__sign" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="acc__body pdp-rte">
          <p>{{ 'product.shipping.estimate' | t }}</p>
          <p>{{ settings.ship_processing | escape }} {{ 'product.shipping.weekdays_then_way' | t }} {{ settings.ship_free_line | escape }}. {{ 'product.shipping.policy_link_intro' | t }} <a href="/policies/shipping-policy">{{ 'product.shipping.policy_link_text' | t }}</a>.</p>
          <p>{{ 'product.returns.window' | t }} <a href="mailto:{{ settings.biz_email }}">{{ settings.biz_email }}</a> {{ 'product.returns.authorization' | t }} {{ 'product.returns.policy_link_intro' | t }} <a href="/policies/refund-policy">{{ 'product.returns.policy_link_text' | t }}</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      {%- comment -%} GPSR (EU 2023/988) safety accordion is disabled by default;
      enable it once manufacturer/safety data is available. {%- endcomment -%}
      {% if false %}
      <details class="acc bb">
        <summary class="acc__q lbl">{{ 'product.tabs.gpsr' | t }}<span class="acc__sign" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="acc__body pdp-rte">{%- render 'pdp-gpsr' -%}</div>
      </details>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} Delivery time sits after the dropdowns, then the two
    remaining trust points (money-back + shipping), then similar products.
    Same settings + locale-fallback pattern as the rest of the buy column — no new
    keys. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign cp_back = settings.guarantee_line -%}
    {%- assign cp_ship = settings.ship_free_line -%}
    {%- unless request.locale.primary -%}
      {%- assign cp_back = 'product.usp.money_back' | t -%}
      {%- assign cp_ship = 'product.usp.shipping' | t -%}
    {%- endunless -%}
    {%- if cp_back != blank or cp_ship != blank -%}
      <div class="pdp-trust-duo lbl-sm">
        {%- if cp_back != blank -%}<span>{% render 'icon', name: 'returns', size: 20 %}<em>{{ cp_back | escape }}</em></span>{%- endif -%}
        {%- if cp_ship != blank -%}<span>{% render 'icon', name: 'truck', size: 20 %}<em>{{ cp_ship | escape }}</em></span>{%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} Complete-the-look renders at the page end — after the
    info accordions, before the related section that the template renders
    next. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- render 'pdp-complete-look', product: product -%}
  </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%} Info list: two columns on every viewport, content swaps
  inline (theme.js), never an accordion and never a page jump. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%} Description is the first info entry. The split first
  paragraph and detail list are both inside it, each exactly once. When no
  split exists, desc_rest already equals the full product.description, so the
  same panel remains lossless. {%- endcomment -%}

  {%- comment -%} Second full-width USP trio is removed entirely — the
  buy-column trio is the only trust trio on the PDP now, both viewports. {%- endcomment -%}

  {%- comment -%} NO BREADCRUMB on the PDP, top or bottom: the bottom
  .pdp__crumbs nav and its styles were deleted outright. Do not reintroduce
  either one. {%- endcomment -%}

  {%- comment -%} THE buy bar. Present from page load on both viewports, carries
  [data-atc] because it IS the add button (no static ATC anywhere above). Inside
  data-product-root so theme.js's scoped queries reach it; position:fixed is
  unaffected — no ancestor creates a containing block.

  Layout: label LEFT, price RIGHT inside the bar. Mechanic: "SELECT A SIZE"
  until a size is picked. Tapping it unpicked opens the expansion panel above
  the bar, which the JS fills by MOVING [data-size-opt] into it — one picker,
  one state, no sync code. {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="pdp__barwrap" data-barwrap>
    <div class="pdp__sheet" data-vsheet hidden>
      <div class="pdp__sheet-head">
        <p class="lbl-sm mute">{{ 'product.atc.select_size' | t }}</p>
        <button type="button" class="hdr__icon" data-vsheet-close aria-label="{{ 'product.size_sheet.close' | t }}">
          {% render 'icon', name: 'close', size: 18 %}
        </button>
      </div>
      <div class="pdp__sheet-slot" data-vsheet-slot></div>
    </div>
    <button
      type="button"
      class="bar pdp__bar{% if needs_size %} bar--awaiting{% endif %}"
      data-atc
      data-variant-id="{% unless needs_size %}{{ v.id }}{% endunless %}"
      {% unless needs_size or v.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
    >
      <span data-atc-label>{% if needs_size %}{{ 'product.atc.select_size' | t }}{% elsif v.available %}{{ 'product.atc.add_to_bag' | t }}{% else %}{{ 'product.atc.sold_out' | t }}{% endif %}</span>
      <span data-atc-price>{% if v.available and needs_size == false %}{{ v.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}{% endif %}</span>
    </button>
    {%- if shop.enabled_payment_types.size > 0 -%}
      <div class="pdp-payments pdp-payments--mobile" aria-label="{{ 'general.accepted_payment_methods' | t }}">
        {%- for payment_type in shop.enabled_payment_types -%}{{ payment_type | payment_type_svg_tag }}{%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} The DESKTOP bar carries more information than a plain
    "SELECT A SIZE" slab: thumbnail, name, colour and price on the left, the
    size row inline in the middle, the ink add block on the right. It only
    appears once the shopper has scrolled PAST the buy column (theme.js
    initBuyBar); the buy column owns the action until then.

    The size buttons here are a SECOND set of [data-opt-btn] elements, not a second
    picker: theme.js's render() paints every [data-opt-btn] on the page and its
    delegated click handler reads every one of them, so this row shares one state with
    the column with no sync code. data-opt-dup marks them so the size recommender only
    ever clicks the column's copy. {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="pdp__richbar" aria-hidden="false">
      <div class="pdp__rb-id">
        {%- if product.featured_media != blank -%}
          <img src="{{ product.featured_media | image_url: width: 120, height: 180, crop: 'center' }}" width="40" height="60" alt="" loading="lazy">
        {%- endif -%}
        <div class="pdp__rb-text">
          <p class="pdp__rb-name lbl">{{ pdp_name | escape }}</p>
          {%- if color_opt_index > -1 -%}
            <p class="pdp__rb-sub lbl-sm">in <span data-opt-current="{{ color_opt_index }}">{{ v.options[color_opt_index] | escape }}</span></p>
          {%- elsif pdp_descriptor != blank -%}
            <p class="pdp__rb-sub lbl-sm">{{ pdp_descriptor | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        <div class="pdp__rb-price lbl">
          <span data-price>
            {%- if v.compare_at_price > v.price -%}
              <s>{{ v.compare_at_price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</s> <span class="price--sale">{{ v.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
            {%- else -%}
              {{ v.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
          <span data-price-badge{% if pdp_price_pct <= 0 %} hidden{% endif %}>{%- if pdp_price_pct > 0 -%}&minus;{{ pdp_price_pct }}%{%- endif -%}</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
        {%- for option in product.options_with_values -%}
          {%- assign rb_down = option.name | downcase -%}
          {%- if rb_down contains 'size' and option.values.size > 1 -%}
            <div class="pdp__rb-sizes">
              <div class="sizes" role="group" aria-label="{{ 'product.option_size' | t }}">
                {%- for value in option.values -%}
                  <button type="button" class="size-btn" data-opt-btn data-opt-dup data-opt-index="{{ forloop.parentloop.index0 }}" data-opt-value="{{ value | escape }}" aria-pressed="{% if needs_size %}false{% elsif v.options[forloop.parentloop.index0] == value %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}">{{ value | escape }}</button>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endunless -%}

      <button
        type="button"
        class="bar pdp__rb-atc{% if needs_size %} bar--awaiting{% endif %}"
        data-atc
        data-variant-id="{% unless needs_size %}{{ v.id }}{% endunless %}"
        {% unless needs_size or v.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
      >
        <span data-atc-label>{% if needs_size %}{{ 'product.atc.select_size' | t }}{% elsif v.available %}{{ 'product.atc.add_to_bag' | t }}{% else %}{{ 'product.atc.sold_out' | t }}{% endif %}</span>
        <span data-atc-price>{% if v.available and needs_size == false %}{{ v.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}{% endif %}</span>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- if size_chart_html != blank -%}
{%- comment -%} data-chart-units drives the client-side unit localization in
standard-extras.js: size-chart headers may be localized
and are converted to inches on imperial locales, at 1 decimal.
data-converted-note replaces the unit note once a conversion actually
happened. {%- endcomment -%}
<dialog
  id="size-chart-dialog"
  class="pdp-sheet"
  aria-label="{{ 'product.size.guide' | t }}"
  data-chart-units="{{ 'product.size_finder.unit_system' | t }}"
  data-converted-note="{{ 'product.size.converted_note' | t | escape }}"
>
  <div class="pdp-sheet__head">
    <h2 class="lbl">{{ 'product.size.guide' | t }}</h2>
    <button type="button" class="hdr__icon" data-close-dialog aria-label="{{ 'product.size_guide.close' | t }}">
      {% render 'icon', name: 'close', size: 20 %}
    </button>
  </div>
  <div class="pdp-sheet__body pdp-rte">
    {{ size_chart_html }}
    {%- if section.settings.size_unit_note != blank -%}<p class="lbl-sm mute" data-size-unit-note>{{ section.settings.size_unit_note | escape }}</p>{%- endif -%}
    {%- comment -%} The size finder lives inside the guide dialog, behind its
    own toggle — one entry point for everything size. Its apply() still
    clicks the real size buttons in the buy column; the dialog stays open so
    the shopper reads the recommendation, the picked size is set behind it. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- render 'size-recommendation' -%}
  </div>
</dialog>
{%- endif -%}

<dialog id="zoom-dialog" class="pdp-zoom" aria-label="{{ 'product.zoom.aria' | t }}">
  <button type="button" class="pdp-zoom__close hdr__icon" data-close-dialog aria-label="{{ 'product.zoom.close' | t }}">
    {% render 'icon', name: 'close', size: 22 %}
  </button>
  <button type="button" class="pdp-zoom__nav pdp-zoom__nav--prev hdr__icon" data-zoom-prev aria-label="{{ 'product.zoom.prev' | t }}">
    {% render 'icon', name: 'arrow', size: 22 %}
  </button>
  <button type="button" class="pdp-zoom__nav pdp-zoom__nav--next hdr__icon" data-zoom-next aria-label="{{ 'product.zoom.next' | t }}">
    {% render 'icon', name: 'arrow', size: 22 %}
  </button>
  <div class="zoom-dialog__inner"><img src="" alt="" width="1024" height="1536"></div>
</dialog>

<script id="product-json" type="application/json">
  {{ product | json }}
</script>

{%- comment -%} jsonld is rendered from layout/theme.liquid for every template — emitting
the Product block here as well would duplicate it. {%- endcomment -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Product page",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "benefit_fallback", "label": "Fallback fact line", "info": "Second fact line under the description when the product has no custom.benefit_line." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "complete_look_collections", "label": "Complete-the-look category collections", "default": "womens-dresses,womens-knitwear,womens-coats-jackets,womens-tops-blouses", "info": "Comma-separated collection handles. The widget shows one piece from each category the current product is NOT in — the Recommendations API alone tends to repeat the same handful of bestsellers storewide." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "enable_size_recommendation", "label": "Size recommendation widget", "default": true, "info": "Height/weight → suggested size, under the size row. Only appears when the product has a size chart (custom.size_table) that parses to a Bust or Hip column." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "size_unit_note", "label": "Size-guide unit note", "default": "All measurements in inches.", "info": "Printed under the size table in the size guide." },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "care_default", "label": "Default fabric & care copy", "info": "Used when the product has no custom.care metafield. Keep it honest — never name a fibre the supplier has not confirmed.", "default": "<p>Machine wash cold on a gentle cycle, inside out. Do not bleach. Line dry or dry flat. Cool iron if needed.</p>" },
    { "type": "html", "id": "size_chart_default", "label": "Default size chart (HTML table)", "info": "Shown in the size guide when the product has no custom.size_table metafield.", "default": "<table><thead><tr><th>Size (US)</th><th>Size (UK)</th><th>Bust</th><th>Waist</th><th>Hip</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>2</td><td>6</td><td>80</td><td>64</td><td>90</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>8</td><td>85</td><td>68</td><td>90</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>10</td><td>90</td><td>72</td><td>90</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>12</td><td>95</td><td>76</td><td>90</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>14</td><td>100</td><td>80</td><td>109</td></tr></tbody></table>" }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
